  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Project Scope**\n\nOkay, I\'m zeroing in on the core of this project: recreating the Favo Gest\303\243o Financeira website. My main objective is to identify how best to highlight the financial consulting services on offer, and to ascertain the critical features for this institutional site\'s update. I\'m focusing on defining the scope and key objectives.\n\n\n**Pinpointing Key Features**\n\nI\'m now identifying the specifics. It seems incorporating GSAP ScrollTrigger, Observer API, and SplitText will be great. Also, fluid transitions with Barba.js, and smooth scrolling with Lenis Scroll are in play. I am designing responsively and with lead conversion in mind, updating the color palette to be more contemporary for financial consulting. The toolset: React with Vite.\n\n\n**Addressing the Technical Challenge**\n\nOkay, here\'s the twist. The Barba.js request has me rethinking the architecture. While React Router + Framer Motion is my usual go-to, I need to reconcile that with the user\'s explicit request for Barba.js. I\'m exploring how to integrate `@barba/core` in a way that feels organic. The split-text requirement has led me to re-evaluate text splitting plugins. The split text plugin is a GSAP club plugin, so I will either look for an open source alternative or build a custom text splitter.\n\n\n**Evaluating Animation Strategy**\n\nI\'ve decided to lean heavily on free tools! I\'ll use `split-type` for text splitting, GSAP\'s Observer and ScrollTrigger, and `@studio-freight/lenis` for smooth scrolling. Barba.js presented a challenge with React, so I\'m considering using React state transitions with GSAP animations or, if necessary, build it in vanilla HTML/JS. Since it\'s a Vite React template, I\'m leaning toward a React SPA with `react-router-dom` and `framer-motion`, which is in the dependencies as `motion`, or using GSAP for page transitions. I\'m also considering a robust single-page scroller, given institutional sites are often single page, and then I will add a router if they want \"page transitions\".\n\n\n**Finalizing the Architecture**\n\nI\'m now integrating the React Router to facilitate those page transitions, leaning heavily on `gsap` for the animations. I will incorporate `lenis` for smooth scrolling, `split-type` for the free text splitting, and also, I\'ll be using `lucide-react` for icons, and Tailwind CSS for styling. The current task is to execute installations and metadata updates. I\'ll focus on getting the React file structure set up.\n\n\n**Defining the Design Elements**\n\nI\'m now nailing down the aesthetic and content structure. I\'ve chosen a dark, modern palette: slate/navy, gold/amber (for \"honey\"), crisp white, and soft grays. The site will have Home, Services (Consulting, Analysis), About, and Contact pages, though fluid transitions might mean a single-page design. On the Home page, I envision a SplitText hero, an Observer API section for data, scroll-triggered service reveals, and a clear CTA. I\'ll utilize tool calls to manage files, install packages, and install `split-type` for the GSAP `SplitText` implementation.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 14
      nanos: 979715766
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
