  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Animation Libraries**\n\nI\'m currently evaluating the request. I need to figure out the best way to do dynamic text animation of the services titles, exploring options beyond the GSAP SplitText library. It\'s premium, so I\'m also looking for similar alternatives. I\'m focusing on open-source solutions or those that have a free-to-use option, if possible.\n\n\n**Implementing Text Animation**\n\nI\'ve decided to use `split-type`, as it functions just like GSAP\'s SplitText and is a free solution for the dynamic text reveal effect I need. I\'m targeting the service titles: \"BPO Financeiro,\" \"Valuation,\" \"Reestrutura\303\247\303\243o,\" and \"M&A (Fus\303\265es),\" within the `.service-card` elements in `/src/pages/Home.tsx`. I\'ll modify the `Home.tsx` file to add a `service-title` class to those titles, then utilize `split-type` within a `useGSAP` block for character-by-character reveal animations triggered by ScrollTrigger.\n\n\n**Synchronizing Animations Refinement**\n\nOkay, I\'m now refining the text animation timing. The goal is a synchronized reveal with the card entry. I\'ll integrate the title animation within the existing `serviceCards.forEach` loop, and I\'m going to create timelines that are more organized and keep everything linked. Specifically, I\'ll be targeting the trigger action alongside the card\'s trigger. I\'ve begun reviewing the `/src/pages/Home.tsx` file to see how it can be implemented.\n\n\n**Refining Timeline Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating the text animation within the `serviceCards` loop. I\'ll modify the loop to incorporate `SplitType` for title splitting and then apply character-by-character reveal animations. This should ensure a synchronized reveal. I\'m focusing on creating timelines linked with the card\'s scroll trigger, for smooth integration.\n\n\n**Adjusting Animation Delays**\n\nI\'m now revising the timing logic. I realize the initial delay on the cards, using `i * 0.15`, will conflict when using ScrollTrigger on a grid layout, where they trigger at the same scroll position. So I\'ll remove the naive stagger and sync the cards. The reveal will have a slight delay after the card fades in. I\'m reviewing `Home.tsx` to reflect these changes.\n\n\n**Optimizing Staggered Delay**\n\nI\'m revisiting the staggered delay implementation for the service cards. The current `delay: i * 0.15` is problematic in a grid layout, causing weird delays. I\'m choosing to trigger the animation based on row, or just apply a stagger to the batch. Or, I could use a timeline. So, I will modify the loop in `/src/pages/Home.tsx` to directly target `.service-card` for a simpler trigger.\n\n\n**Finalizing Synchronization Logic**\n\nI\'m now putting the finishing touches on the animation logic. I\'ve integrated a timeline that reveals the title in the service cards. The timeline is set up to overlap the card\'s animation. I\'m focusing on the trigger action alongside the card\'s trigger. I\'ve just been reviewing the `/src/pages/Home.tsx` file for implementation.\n\n\n**Refining 3D Rotation**\n\nI\'ve just considered the impact of `split-type` on the layout and decided that since the titles are block elements, it should be fine. I\'m choosing to go with a `y` and `opacity` reveal for the text animation for a clean look, rather than using the perspective or 3D rotation. I\'m revisiting `/src/pages/Home.tsx` to refine the `useGSAP` hook and consider the card animations.\n\n\n**Refining Title Animation**\n\nI\'m now integrating the updated timeline with character reveals for each service title. I\'ve re-written the card animation to use stagger and have added the title animation. The titles will have a slight delay after the card fades in. I\'m focusing on making sure the delays and timing are responsive. I\'ve been making further reviews to `/src/pages/Home.tsx` to finalize the animation.\n\n\n"
