  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Developing Magnetic Button**\n\nI\'ve decided to create `src/components/MagneticButton.tsx` and have started the implementation. The button will use `gsap` for animation. The CTA \"Fale Conosco\" is in `Header.tsx` which will be useful as a reference. I\'m going to start with the design of the base button.\n\n\n**Implementing Magnetism Effect**\n\nI\'ve crafted the `MagneticButton` component and added GSAP for the animation. I\'ve hooked up the mouse move event listeners to the component, which is now responding to mouse movements, and the mouseleave event handler is returning it to the default position. I\'m focusing on the magnetism effect. I\'m leveraging `gsap.quickTo` for a smoother response.\n\n\n**Refining Button Implementation**\n\nI\'m reconsidering the inline-block div wrapper for `MagneticButton`. It might interfere with the child\'s sizing if it assumes it fills the container. Analyzing the `Home.tsx` button shows it\'s a flex item, so wrapping it shouldn\'t cause issues. The next step is to figure out how `MagneticButton` will animate its child component, not the wrapper.\n\n\n**Revising Animation Technique**\n\nI\'m now thinking about how the animation works with the button\'s structure. If I animate the `div` wrapper, the child element also moves. I\'m using `gsap.quickTo` on the wrapper, so this is expected. I am now considering if passing the ref directly to the child element is possible to avoid the nested wrappers. No, inline-block or inline-flex is still standard, so I should stick to that, or I can use React `cloneElement`.\n\n\n**Testing CloneElement Strategy**\n\nI\'ve decided to test the `cloneElement` approach directly, since `Link` and the underlying `<a>` tag both support ref-forwarding. This will avoid any unnecessary wrapper elements and keep the component structure clean. I will proceed by implementing this technique and reviewing the results.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 10
      nanos: 932425071
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
