  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Component**\n\nI\'m currently focused on dissecting the request. My initial goal is understanding the \"Onboarding Journey\" component for the \"Gest\303\243o Financeira\" page. I\'ve begun to conceptualize a step-by-step progress graphic aimed at gamifying the process. The core idea is to visually communicate the speed and simplicity of the client\'s transition.\n\n\n**Developing the Visuals**\n\nNow, I\'m fleshing out Component 1, aiming for an elegant onboarding timeline using GSAP. I\'ve defined four clear steps: Kickoff, System Setup, Access Transition, and Autopilot. Considering a horizontal design with animated connecting lines, and I\'m playing with a clean aesthetic: light background, dark text, and golden accents. Component 2 will be a GSAP-powered animated counter for impact metrics. I\'ll trigger the animation using ScrollTrigger when the element is visible.\n\n\n**Planning the Implementation**\n\nMy focus has shifted to the implementation. I\'m strategizing how to integrate the components into `GestaoFinanceira.tsx`, considering placement after the Hero section and Tasks Grid. I\'ll start by creating the `AnimatedCounter` and `OnboardingJourney` components, then adjust the main page. I\'ve drafted `AnimatedCounter.tsx`, using GSAP and ScrollTrigger for the animated counter, ready to connect the proxy object\'s value to the DOM.\n\n\n**Refining the Animation**\n\nI\'m now refining the GSAP animation logic for the counter, ensuring smooth transitions. I\'ve focused on mapping over the metrics and creating refs for each number, and I\'m using GSAP to animate them. I\'m aiming for a visually appealing and engaging counter that effectively showcases the impact metrics. I\'m also ensuring the counter triggers correctly with ScrollTrigger.\n\n\n**Optimizing the Animation**\n\nI\'m now revising the animation for a better user experience. To handle number formatting and suffixes, I\'ve decided a proxy object is superior. I\'m focusing on the logic within GSAP and how it translates to the display, prioritizing a clean, standalone `ImpactMetrics.tsx` component. This new setup will ensure proper formatting for values such as \"2.500\".\n\n\n**Constructing the Components**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `ImpactMetrics` component. I\'ve integrated `ScrollTrigger` and GSAP for animated counters, incorporating a data structure for metrics. I\'m focusing on the animation logic to accurately render the different values. Next, I\'ll build the `OnboardingJourney` component using a flexible design that adapts to mobile and desktop displays.\n\n\n**Positioning the Components**\n\nI\'ve decided to place the `ImpactMetrics` component directly after the Hero section for an immediate trust-building impact. Subsequently, the `OnboardingJourney` component will be positioned after the Tasks Grid, preceding the \"Tangible Results\" section. I\'ll implement these component placements shortly.\n\nI\'m now refining the ImpactMetrics.tsx file, including the use of GSAP\'s proxy object to ensure proper number formatting using `Intl.NumberFormat(\'pt-BR\').format(val)`. I am also working on the counter\'s animation to make sure the scroll trigger works accordingly.\n\n\n**Finalizing the Visuals**\n\nI\'m now implementing the visuals for the `OnboardingJourney`. I\'ve constructed the component with an array of step objects, including icons, titles and descriptions. I\'m aiming for a horizontal layout with animated connecting lines, leveraging GSAP and ScrollTrigger for a dynamic user experience. My priority now is to ensure seamless integration and appropriate responsiveness, including the use of lucide-react icons.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 35
      nanos: 474045741
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
