  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the User\'s Input**\n\nI\'m now focused on the user\'s initial request. I\'ve broken down the value propositions, specifically \"Efficient Organization,\" \"Saving Time and Resources,\" and \"Reduced Default Rates\". I\'m starting to build a basic framework to connect these benefits to the underlying service, but have not added further propositions.\n\n\n**Integrating New Propositions**\n\nI am now integrating the new value propositions: \"Vis\303\243o Estrat\303\251gica,\" \"Apoio Especializado,\" and \"Liberdade Financeira.\" My current plan is to add a \"Benef\303\255cios\" section to the `Gest\303\243o Financeira` page, likely before or after the features grid. I\'m leaning toward a grid layout, possibly two or three columns with icons to complement the premium feel.\n\n\n**Refining Content and Structure**\n\nI\'m now refining the \"Benef\303\255cios\" section content and considering different titles, like \"Muito al\303\251m dos n\303\272meros.\" I\'ve selected icons like `FolderCheck` for \"Organiza\303\247\303\243o Eficiente,\" aiming for elegance. I\'m focusing on concisely conveying each benefit and linking them visually. I\'m also preparing to add specialized support content.\n\n\n**Implementing the New Section**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in the implementation phase. I\'ve decided to create a new component, `FinancialBenefits.tsx`, for a cleaner `GestaoFinanceira.tsx`. I\'ve mapped out icons using `lucide-react`, focusing on `Layers` for Efficient Organization, `Clock` for Time and Resource Savings, and `ShieldCheck` for Reduced Default Rates, among others. I\'m also planning to use GSAP with ScrollTrigger for a revealing animation to enhance the section\'s impact. I also decided on some new icons for the new value propositions, adding `Users` for Specialized Support and `Unlock` for Financial Freedom.\n\n\n**Expanding the Iconography**\n\nI am now expanding the iconography to include more specialized choices, to ensure each benefit is visually distinct. I\'ve just added the `Target` icon for \"Strategic Vision,\" and I\'ve also incorporated the `Coffee` icon to represent \"Tranquilidade.\" I\'m aiming for a cohesive and intuitive visual language that complements the textual descriptions.\n\n\n**Refining UI Component Logic**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into refining the `FinancialBenefits` UI component logic. I\'ve re-reviewed the benefit cards\' data structure, ensuring each icon\'s association is accurate and accessible. I\'m now implementing the GSAP animation for the benefit cards. I am utilizing `useRef` and `useGSAP` for animation control. I\'m optimizing the trigger to enhance the visual impact.\n\n\n**Implementing Animation Triggers**\n\nI\'m now focusing on optimizing the animation triggers, to create a smooth user experience. I\'m focusing on refining the `ScrollTrigger` setup within the `useGSAP` hook, and I\'m ensuring the animation starts and ends at the optimal scroll positions. I\'m also now adjusting the delay of the animation in relation to other animations in the component.\n\n\n**Integrating the Final Component**\n\nI\'m now integrating the `FinancialBenefits` component into `GestaoFinanceira.tsx`. I\'ve added the necessary import statement and placed the component between the Tasks grid and the Onboarding Journey sections. I\'m confirming that the page structure and the new section are well-aligned, and I am ensuring that the component responds correctly within the existing layout.\n\n\n**Verifying Benefit Details**\n\nI\'m now meticulously reviewing the provided text to ensure 100% accurate transcription of the value propositions. Specifically, I am confirming the correct translation and the exact phrasing for each benefit. I am ensuring that the Portuguese benefits align with the descriptions that I\'ve been working with. I\'m focusing on \"Organiza\303\247\303\243o Eficiente,\" \"Economia de Tempo e Recursos,\" \"Redu\303\247\303\243o de Inadimpl\303\252ncia,\" \"Vis\303\243o Estrat\303\251gica,\" and \"Apoio Especializado.\"\n\n\n"
