    thinking: "**Reviewing Integration Points**\n\nI\'m currently focused on dissecting the user\'s goal. I\'m pinpointing the exact integration points for the new Favo copy, identifying potential objections, and strategizing urgency triggers. Simultaneously, I\'m ensuring the previously established benefits in `FinancialBenefits.tsx` are effectively reiterated.\n\n\n**Analyzing New Content**\n\nI\'ve been given some new content: an intro, urgency triggers, and a transition piece. I\'m assessing how these elements resonate with the established framework. I\'m particularly interested in how they can be used to underscore the importance of financial management, using the urgency/risk triggers to highlight the critical need for an effective system. I\'m looking at how these new pieces fit within the context, specifically in terms of tone and impact.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Risk Integration**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing the placement of the risk information. The ideal spot seems to be within `GestaoFinanceira.tsx`, strategically positioning it before the established benefits, creating a compelling narrative. I\'m carefully reviewing the flow of `GestaoFinanceira.tsx`, and how best to introduce risks before the benefits already in place. I\'m also considering an alternative placement, in `Home.tsx`, and will analyze pros and cons of both options.\n\n\n**Evaluating Risk Placement**\n\nOkay, I\'ve decided where to place the risk information. The \"Problem Awareness\" section from the prompt is perfect for addressing objections. I\'m going to create a `RiskAwareness.tsx` component and insert it into `GestaoFinanceira.tsx`, right before `FinancialBenefits.tsx`. This approach builds the problem and then provides the solution. I\'m confident it will set the stage effectively.\n\n\n**Constructing Risk Component**\n\nOkay, I\'m making progress on `RiskAwareness.tsx`. I\'ve crafted the title and subtitle, and added the four key risk cards. The bottom text is in place as well. The tone is set to be somewhat urgent. I\'m also considering a darker background section with light text for this component to create a visual \"warning\" cue. I\'m also planning to incorporate GSAP animations to add to the urgency.\n\n\n**Crafting Risk Component**\n\nI\'m now integrating the risk cards with Lucide icons. I\'ve also finalized the section\'s visual elements, opting for a dark green/black background (`#232A1B`), off-white text (`#F7F6EE`), and gold accents (`#D8B36B`). The intro block\'s highlighted quote is now in place. I\'ve also crafted the section heading and the individual card content, focusing on the potential consequences of poor financial management. The first two risk card are complete: \"Total Desorganiza\303\247\303\243o com o Financeiro\" and \"Inadimpl\303\252ncia e Problemas de Pagamento\". I\'ll create two more risk cards, and finalize animations.\n\n\n**Finalizing Risk Awareness**\n\nI\'ve completed the remaining risk cards: \"Maiores Riscos de Fraude e Erros\" and \"Perda de Oportunidades de Crescimento\", and the GSAP animations are in place. I have concluded by inserting a concluding statement and the `RiskAwareness.tsx` component into `GestaoFinanceira.tsx`, before `TangibleResults`, as per the flow of 1. Hero, 2. Risk Awareness (The Problem), 3. Financial Benefits (The Solution/Benefits).\n\n\n\n"
