d and replace to ensure the color changes. After this, I checked the contrast of `#4e653d` on `#fffff0`. The luminance checks out, with about 5:1 or 6:1 contrast ratio, so I am safe to use it for body text. Headings are getting `#472f5b`, which will have excellent contrast. Now, I am updating the files listed, which includes `src/App.tsx`, `src/components/Footer.tsx` and the rest.\n\n\n**Automating the Updates**\n\nI\'m now automating the global replacements across multiple files using `find` and `sed`. I\'ve prepared bulk replace commands to update the background, main text, and body text colors across all relevant `.tsx` and `.ts` files. I am cautiously running these commands, and I\'ll review any `git diff` output to verify the changes, and I\'ve also prepared the replacement for hover text effects, replacing `#D8B36B` with `#866428`.\n\n\n"
