  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Implementing Smooth Scrolling**\n\nI\'ve decided to implement smooth scrolling using a global event listener that targets clicks on anchor links (`a[href^=\"#\"]`). I\'ll grab the hash from the link and use Lenis\'s `scrollTo(hash)` method. This should provide a clean and smooth user experience.\n\n\n**Refining Scroll Interception**\n\nI\'ve refined the click handler. I am now checking `target.pathname` against `window.location.pathname`. This ensures smooth scrolling only happens when the user clicks an anchor on the same page, preventing unintended behavior with React Router\'s `<Link>` components. The logic now correctly intercepts internal hash navigations.\n\n\n**Addressing React Router Interaction**\n\nI\'ve realized a new edge case with React Router. Navigating from `/gestao-financeira#contato` to `/` via a link requires special handling. React Router\'s default behavior doesn\'t auto-scroll to the hash on page load. I\'ll need to use `useEffect` to listen to changes in `location.hash` or `location.pathname` and scroll with `lenis.scrollTo(location.hash)`. I also need to make sure to handle `AnimatePresence`\'s `onExitComplete` which does a `window.scrollTo(0, 0)` \342\200\223 potentially cancelling scroll on load. The goal remains smooth scrolling throughout the application.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 555515340
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
