    summary: "Lottie animations are typically lightweight, vector animations stored in a JSON-based file format. These files describe shapes and motion as data, making them scalable and efficient for web and app use[1][2][3]. While the specific instructions for \"lottie.host\" were not found, most Lottie hosting platforms provide a way to download the animation as a `.json` file.\n\nGenerally, to obtain a Lottie `.json` file from a hosting service like LottieFiles, Lottielab, or Tiiny.host, you would typically follow these steps:\n1.  **Locate the animation:** Find the specific Lottie animation you wish to download on the platform[4].\n2.  **Look for export/download options:** Search for an \"Export\" or \"Download\" button or a similar option within the animation\'s details or editor interface[4][5][6].\n3.  **Select Lottie (JSON) format:** In the export or download panel, ensure that \"Lottie (JSON)\" or \".json\" is selected as the desired file format[4][5][6].\n4.  **Initiate download:** Click the \"Download\" button to save the `.json` file to your device[4][5].\n\nSome platforms also support a newer, compressed format called `.lottie`, which bundles one or more animations and their assets into a smaller file[1][3]. Additionally, browser extensions exist that can help extract Lottie animations directly from live websites as `.json` or `.lottie` files[7].\n\nSources:\n[1] [dreamhost.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQENYT4DanS4ZugKOGIOBy4i0_tKvhyD5fQo9NhDySTw-I4V-O4MBUDvJ59JoyYxchdqwJ_34Z8dXNYnvZFxkz8LAW6OQdgm6hYAgu6384sPwUJCQ-KXCrBXVesOLH3alYRDU8AK_Kgl9RhyPM9CYuXy)\n[2] [github.io](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEFMppKuVGxVRKgnG5XtfQhWk6F8eM7UYEyu1sJ0cfnYMy3uaGH4s7OG8lb5zx_ghC330ROrawGuC_dX1dWfA6b4wEdQQ9x3FuzJOGO2TCk4WBYUHg=)\n[3] [unicornicons.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHaAWu2ixQ8uiwsNEksFRhN44LFql1KxpXyT7C1NAw4KlT2R3uNhkaih6mjf_ANS1CdhURcPjgssv3nsQxGiLvJIbmZDZDzGVucVzqWRuPniu9do-tcrGQH8rCgpC1nvOz5gjBD6iEJWA==)\n[4] [lottielab.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHF8KxpO_mLTwui9hwTScIUt8ckKq7BMC0YQ0BL43SkPfJE9Ue9HLr1Gz0vPIeC6ADkGqjsb3e08C2__8ubac5QKs1dZfCmKCTRHsWcUW2MMyg4KT-W9But-o--AiZIdgvLpi_SaosdoVBOpLpZ7UJonzYD00UdoX0j-MoYCSMUrsvkPR0Xv68GgzsyQg==)\n[5] [linearity.io](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGUEEM-lY8k3Y74vLVmcU634u9F7SZMjbumRyMnxLCEb4ZD7kRSt-kh0qYh-0jHC2aDyASV0rqu6CTiDmVmU0fFr6RchE8bvdkGP6kDlOPlP1cGFDO-SPB2TFNudmdsturlyil5hnbnTsKnmILPBOwRGd-OjQcLGoPBE08wBrYq5YiVEeyIBBF4rrM9)\n[6] [youtube.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHKzjhxzl0a52B7or9fqYY006ZiIgp-oK5PR-OElT9PUQZSkNnfhdL1h_6-BOCqRvezk_iNACZ5pwZRikjynqnpa21eS8rA-5dk5sxXe3s-YZx72BS22tTMGO8O7G3ku8zm_DCbfZo=)\n[7] [miromiro.app](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFZlObeA2qYuk3Cd4xjXowIIALqu3UEJZQ8bPJxYXItxUsHz7DXVozGpYTnDhY-0BJUVjr3X06NABqmJbwLxgWdSXSHXaWnCXBDUJs9GbmeCpOmhOk-N0mOqvN4rXgTNQcza4ucrgVEEMtvBx8hLGiRvl7C-tC4yWXS0Q==)"
