  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the FAQ Component**\n\nOkay, I\'m now zeroing in on the `/src/components/FAQ.tsx` file. I\'m taking stock of its current form. My goal is to add more detailed explanations to the FAQ section, and to pre-emptively address objections users might have. I need to figure out the best way to integrate these without sacrificing the component\'s cleanness.\n\n\n**Expanding the FAQ\'s Scope**\n\nI\'ve got a list of five key questions already addressed in the FAQ. Now, I\'m focusing on expanding its scope. I\'m actively brainstorming additional objections and questions users might have. These include cost concerns, tooling adaptability, company size suitability, daily communication methods, and mitigating potential mistakes. I\'m currently working to develop compelling responses.\n\n\n**Formulating New Entries**\n\nI\'ve just translated and drafted some new FAQ entries in Portuguese, matching the brand\'s tone. The questions address potential client concerns about the cost of outsourcing finance compared to hiring in-house staff, and whether they need to change their existing financial software. I\'ve focused on concise, persuasive answers to each, highlighting the benefits of our approach and alleviating their concerns.\n\n\n**Refining the Portuguese FAQs**\n\nI\'ve just refined the latest Portuguese FAQ entries. I\'ve focused on addressing concerns about applicability for smaller businesses, ensuring responsive daily communication with clients, and reassuring clients that there are checks in place in case of mistakes. The goal is now to polish these answers to ensure they are as clear and persuasive as possible.\n\n\n"
