    thinking: "**Considering UI Integrity**\n\nI\'m thinking more about the `tasks-grid` element in `GestaoFinanceira.tsx`. I need to ensure any changes maintain its current GSAP animation. I can wrap it, but I shouldn\'t alter it, except when implementing the requested \"fade-in-up\" animations via Framer Motion for all elements, as per specifications.\n\n\n**Implementing Fade-In Effects**\n\nOkay, I\'ve got a plan to implement the \"fade-in-up\" animations. I\'m thinking of wrapping the main page sections with `<FadeInUp>`. I\'m a little concerned about GSAP conflicts, since sections could be animating in via Framer Motion *and* have child GSAP animations that depend on scroll position. However, since the GSAP animation\'s vertical displacement `y: 40` isn\'t huge, it should be fine. Worst-case scenario, I can adjust `refreshPriority` or wrap only certain components. I think I\'ll start by wrapping sections with `<FadeInUp>` directly.\n\n\n**Refactoring with Sections**\n\nI\'m now shifting gears to refactoring the section wrappers. Creating a custom `<Section>` component seems the most efficient approach. I\'ll build it in `src/components/Section.tsx`, incorporating the `framer-motion` animations. This should allow me to replace all those standard `section` and `div` wrappers with the new `<Section>` component. It\'ll simplify things and maintain consistency.\n\n\n"
