  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Testing the implementation**\n\nI\'m thinking of creating a `CustomCursor.tsx` component. I plan to use `framer-motion` to make the cursor track smoothly. I\'ll also use `Math.atan2` for rotation, ensuring it faces the correct direction. That will be very cool!\n\n\n**Implementing the BeeCursor**\n\nI\'m now creating `src/components/BeeCursor.tsx` to get this rolling. I\'m leveraging `framer-motion` for smooth movement and spring animations. I\'m also using `useMotionValue` for tracking mouse position and calculating the rotation for the bee icon. A `useEffect` hook handles mouse move events and visibility toggling.\n\n\n**Refining the Rotation Logic**\n\nI\'ve refined the rotation logic for the cursor. I\'m using `Math.atan2` to calculate the angle and converting it to degrees. To prevent continuous spinning, I\'m handling the rotation wrapping by calculating the shortest path difference and updating the `rotation` value accordingly. I\'m also tracking mouse position using `e.clientX` and `e.clientY`. Finally, I\'ve added event listeners for `mousemove`, `mouseleave`, and `mouseenter` events to control cursor visibility.\n\n\n**Optimizing the Implementation**\n\nI\'m now focusing on optimizing the cursor component for touch devices. I\'ve added a check to hide the cursor if the device has a coarse pointer. This prevents the cursor from displaying on touchscreens, enhancing the user experience. I\'ve also incorporated the SVG for the bee, adjusting the `translate` properties to correctly position it relative to the cursor coordinates.\n\n\n**Adjusting the Cursor Logic**\n\nI\'m now revising the CSS. The initial implementation with `cursor: none !important` was too broad and affected text selection. I\'m modifying the CSS to target the `body` and possibly links for cursor hiding, keeping the custom bee cursor following the real mouse pointer. The bee will act as the cursor.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 21
      nanos: 610425116
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
