moving `div` elements to a container ref for a purely visual effect. This is a far more performant choice for this type of effect.\n\n\n**Finalizing the DOM Implementation**\n\nI\'m now fully committed to the Vanilla JS DOM approach for this pollen effect. I\'m focusing on the `BeeCursor.tsx` file and am implementing the `createPollen` function to dynamically generate `div` elements representing the pollen particles. Each pollen particle\'s size and position will be randomized, with a transition for a smooth visual effect. I\'m also ensuring a slight opacity for a more appealing aesthetic.\n\n\n"
